From 86853050d2115e1779c3eec26c8f1852a1dcf54b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:42:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(catalog): add the turning case cone-thread - a cone
 with a threaded end

The case examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread turns a 30 mm bar to a
20 mm to 10 mm cone with a neck and an M10x1.5 thread, on the built-in
2-axis lathe with the Fanuc lathe post: face, rough profile, finish
profile, neck groove, thread (G32 passes), part-off.

The profile operations cut to a turned-blank model and the neck, thread
and part-off cut to the finished model, because Profile Finish reads the
thread valleys and the neck step as rest (issue 2880). The thread posts
as G32 passes, because a G76 cycle would start inside the part (issues
2878 and 2879). The shoulder is sharp, because a fillet sends the
profile rides far out of the bar (issue 2881).

Pinned by example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread
and the two suite tests that iterate all catalog cases.

Fixes #2394

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
